Rust Day 5: Constants & shadowing, explained line by line. Same name, new value, and why mut can't do what shadowing does.

📌 In this short:
✅ const: always immutable, type required, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE, value known at compile time
✅ Shadowing: let x = x + 1 makes a NEW x; inner scopes shadow until the block ends
✅ Shadowing can change the type; mut can't (error E0308: mismatched types)

💻 Code from the video:
const MAX_SCORE: u32 = 100_000;

fn main() {
    let x = 5;
    let x = x + 1;
    {
        let x = x * 2;
        println!("inner: {x}"); // 12
    }
    println!("outer: {x}"); // 6
}

📖 Learn more: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch03-01-variables-and-mutability.html
